# Personal data — never publish. Allowlist approach deliberately, not a named
# blocklist: naming excluded topic folders here would itself leak what they're
# about to anyone reading this file in the public repo. Everything under
# session_summaries/ is ignored by default; only the project's own dev-history
# folder is explicitly let back in.
session_summaries/*
!session_summaries/memory-project/

# CLAUDE.md itself is also excluded: it's this machine's real operational doc
# (real corpus scope, real absolute paths, real excluded topics). The public-
# facing docs are README.md and CLAUDE.md.example instead.
CLAUDE.md
local_config.py
.chromadb/
.auto_capture_state.json
.recall_session_cache
activity.log
backlink_errors/

# Environment
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS
.DS_Store

# Local Claude Code project settings (intentionally empty — hooks are global, see CLAUDE.md)
.claude/
